# Copy this file to .env.integration before running `bun run test:integration`.
#
#   cp .env.integration.example .env.integration
#
# `.env.integration` is gitignored, so a fresh clone or a new git worktree does not
# have one. `bun --env-file=` silently ignores a missing file, so without this
# copy the integration suites fall back to Bun's SQL defaults and fail with an
# opaque `database "<your-unix-user>" does not exist`. `bun run preflight` runs
# first and catches that.
#
# This lived at `test-app/.env` until test-app was removed. It is repo-level
# now because it always described the FRAMEWORK's test services, not any one
# app's — nothing here should depend on an app that may be deleted.

# Postgres used by the FSR store, list store, notify/watcher and sync-triggers
# suites. The role needs CREATE TABLE on this database — the suites create and
# drop their own fixtures. Any local database works; it does not have to be
# named `kilnjs_test`.
#
# Use a database of its own, NOT one an app also uses: the catch-up cursor is
# fleet-shared (ADR-022), so a dev server on the same Postgres consumes the
# invalidation events these suites are waiting for and they fail on timeouts
# that look exactly like code regressions.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/kilnjs_test

# Redis used by RedisCache and the hub pub/sub suites.
# Pick a dedicated logical DB: Kiln cache keys (kiln:html:/, ...) are namespaced
# only when an app sets cache.namespace, so two Kiln targets sharing db 0
# collide on shared routes like "/".
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1

# Named `.env.integration`, NOT `.env.test`: `bun test` sets NODE_ENV=test and
# Bun auto-loads `.env.test` from the cwd, which would leak DATABASE_URL into
# `bun run test:unit` and make 16 app DB suites run against the wrong database.
